---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Privacy policy | Registry Stack';
const pageDescription =
  'What registrystack.org collects, why, and what it does not do: analytics, email correspondence, server logs, your rights, and the effective date.';
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <SiteHeader current="privacy" />

  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="privacy-hero-title">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
          <h1 id="privacy-hero-title">Privacy policy</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            This page explains what registrystack.org collects, why, and what it does not do. It
            covers this website only. The hosted lab at lab.registrystack.org and the docs site at
            docs.registrystack.org are separate services with their own policies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="privacy-body-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="legal-body">
          <h2 id="privacy-who-title">Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            Registry Stack is published by Aubex Consulting LLC, 28 Geary St, Ste 650 #189, San
            Francisco, CA 94108, United States. Aubex is the controller responsible for this
            website. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:contact@registrystack.org">contact@registrystack.org</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-collect-title">What this site collects</h2>
          <p>
            This site is a static set of pages. It has no accounts, no forms, and it does not set
            any cookies of its own.
          </p>
          <h3>Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            We run a self-hosted analytics tool, Umami, at stats.registrystack.org. It is
            cookie-free. When it is enabled, it records aggregate, de-identified usage data: page
            views, referring sites, and a general browser and device class. It does not build a
            profile of an individual visitor and does not share data with advertising networks. We
            also tag some outbound link clicks, for example to the docs site, the live demo, or
            GitHub, with the link&rsquo;s destination and label, so we can see which resources
            visitors use next. These events are not tied to a name, an email address, or any other
            identifying detail.
          </p>
          <h3>Email</h3>
          <p>
            If you email us, you give us your address and the content of your message. We use that
            only to reply to you and keep the exchange as ordinary business correspondence.
          </p>
          <h3>Server logs</h3>
          <p>
            This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub, as the hosting provider, keeps its own
            server logs, for example request IP addresses, to operate the service. We do not
            configure or query those logs beyond what GitHub provides. GitHub&rsquo;s own privacy
            statement covers that data.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-not-title">What this site does not do</h2>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>It does not set cookies of its own.</li>
            <li>It does not run advertising and does not share data with ad networks.</li>
            <li>It does not sell personal data.</li>
            <li>It does not build behavioral profiles of visitors.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="privacy-basis-title">Legal bases for visitors in the EEA and UK</h2>
          <p>
            Where the GDPR or the UK GDPR applies, we rely on legitimate interest to run
            aggregate, cookie-free analytics that help us understand which pages are useful. If
            you email us, that exchange proceeds on the basis that you chose to contact us and
            provided your information for that purpose.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-retention-title">Retention</h2>
          <p>
            Analytics events are aggregate and are not tied to an identified person. We keep them
            only as long as they are useful for understanding site usage. Email correspondence is
            kept as ordinary business records for as long as it stays relevant.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-rights-title">Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can ask us to access, correct, or delete personal data you have given us, for
            example the content of an email, by writing to <a href="mailto:contact@registrystack.org">contact@registrystack.org</a>.
            We will respond. Aggregate analytics data is not tied to an identified person, so there
            is generally nothing to look up or erase per visitor. If you believe otherwise in your
            case, tell us and we will look into it.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-third-party-title">Third-party services linked from this site</h2>
          <p>
            This site links to GitHub for source code and releases, to docs.registrystack.org for
            documentation, and to lab.registrystack.org, a hosted demo that runs on synthetic data
            only. Each of those is a separate service with its own privacy practices. This policy
            covers registrystack.org only.
          </p>

          <h2 id="privacy-changes-title">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this page as the site changes. The effective date below tells you when
            it last changed.
          </p>

          <p class="legal-effective">Effective date: July 4, 2026.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-body {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-body h2 {
    margin-top: 44px;
  }

  .legal-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal-body h3 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .legal-body p {
    color: var(--registry-body);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .legal-body .check-list {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  .legal-effective {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-rule);
    color: var(--registry-muted);
    margin-top: 44px;
    padding-top: 20px;
  }
</style>
